{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Sarai was barren.</b> It is difficult: 'she had no child' — why do I need it? And one answers that it was necessary to say that she did not even have a place for the emergence of the child, as we say: Abraham and Sarah were tumtumin and were torn open, as it is said: ״הביטו אל צור חצבתם ואל מקבת בור נקרתם״. Another explanation: she does not have now, and she will have after a time, as we say: ותהר ותלד שרה, and similar to this: וכל אשר אין לו סנפיר וקשקשת — we derive in tractate חולין: it does not have now, and is destined to grow after a time."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:15.796064358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}